  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Your Python function remembers data from the last call?"
  },
  {
   "id": "bug",
   "text": "Most devs blame the cache here."
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "text": "But default arguments are created once, when the function is defined, so every call shares the same list."
  },
  {
   "id": "fix",
   "text": "Default to None, then create a new list inside the function. Three calls, three fresh lists, zero leaked data."
  },
  {
   "id": "bait",
   "text": "Have you hit this bug before? Comment yes or no."
  },
  {
   "id": "follow",
